{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/26","id":5024297439,"node_id":"PR_kwDON1sLX88AAAABK3ix3w","html_url":"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/26","diff_url":"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/26.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/pull/26.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/26","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/26/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/26/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/issues/26/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/konard/konard.github.io/statuses/09160c7099d84858dbc19a301451b9d2d4337c1c","number":26,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Improve automatic spacing, sharp arrow geometry and per-link editing","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #25\n\nAutomatic spacing now discovers gaps for `2222` without manual setup and measures the painted shafts and markers, including stroke width and configurable clearance. Sharp arrows keep acute tips and balance their painted endpoints by default; rounded, bevelled and inherited corners and legacy lengths remain selectable. Each link now has a responsive card containing all nine existing inputs, with visible gap overrides.\n\nThe shared geometry serves the preview, solver, SVG and raster exports. Gallery/rain defaults and existing link actions are preserved. Optional solver diagnostics default off. The bounded search remains heuristic: unattainable clearance within the configured bounds retains its residual score.\n\n### Reproduction and verification\n\n- Original failure: open `/network/?code=2222&rotation=90&solve=true&lang=en`. The original drawing collapses near the referenced middle. Automatic mode now finds both reference gaps and reduces the fixture's painted score from about 7.4386 to 0.\n- Reference arrangement: `/network/?code=2222&rotation=90&turns=15+-15&gaps=0.18+0.18+%7E+%7E&lang=en`. Equal gaps now produce balanced painted extents. The same fixture at `endAngle=5` keeps its sharp tip.\n- `node experiments/issue-25-reproduce.mjs` runs the new tests against the original source and restores current files: all six issue regressions fail as expected. A seventh regression protects the zero-gap fallback discovered during implementation.\n- 717 unit tests; ESLint, formatting, file limits, secret scan, dependency audit, production build and all 120 CV PDFs.\n- Native Chromium, Firefox and WebKit checks cover sharp endpoints at 5°/15°/45°, exact Apply/share/reload SVG equality, card editing/removal and English/Russian mobile layout. The raster check supersamples acute tips while retaining the same normalized tolerance.\n- Existing editor/download, issue 19, issue 21 and issue 23 suites remain in the three-engine CI matrix, including the full 4131-card gallery and actual compositor checks. Local compatibility checks run sequentially within the container budget.\n\n[Detailed case study, requirement map, chronology, research and alternatives](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-25-665823cdf9ad/docs/case-studies/issue-25/README.md), [validation and archived logs/data](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-25-665823cdf9ad/docs/case-studies/issue-25/VALIDATION.md).\n\nFinal CI [40404466882](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/actions/runs/40404466882) passed for `09160c7099d84858dbc19a301451b9d2d4337c1c` (created 2026-10-26 21:27:10 UTC): all checks, 717 tests, five browser suites in each of Chromium/Firefox/macOS WebKit, the production build and all 120 CV PDFs. The complete logs and browser evidence from source run [40401691502](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/actions/runs/40401691502) are archived in the case study. Final review confirmed that `main` is an ancestor, there are no outstanding issue/PR comments, and the working tree is clean.\n\n### Visual evidence\n\nAutomatic mode, before and after:\n\n| Before | After |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Before: collapsed automatic drawing](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-25-665823cdf9ad/docs/case-studies/issue-25/screenshots/before-auto.png?raw=true) | ![After: automatically spaced painted shapes](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-25-665823cdf9ad/docs/case-studies/issue-25/screenshots/chromium-after-auto.png?raw=true) |\n\nBalanced endpoints and acute tips:\n\n| Before | After |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Before: unequal manual endpoints](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-25-665823cdf9ad/docs/case-studies/issue-25/screenshots/before-manual.png?raw=true) | ![After: balanced sharp endpoints](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-25-665823cdf9ad/docs/case-studies/issue-25/screenshots/chromium-after-manual.png?raw=true) |\n| ![Before: acute tip is lost](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-25-665823cdf9ad/docs/case-studies/issue-25/screenshots/before-acute.png?raw=true) | ![After: acute tip remains sharp](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-25-665823cdf9ad/docs/case-studies/issue-25/screenshots/chromium-after-acute.png?raw=true) |\n\nPer-link controls, before and after:\n\n| Before | After |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Before: table and separate gap disclosure](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-25-665823cdf9ad/docs/case-studies/issue-25/screenshots/before-editor.png?raw=true) | ![After: cards with every link input](https://github.com/konard/konard.github.io/blob/issue-25-665823cdf9ad/docs/case-studies/issue-25/screenshots/chromium-after-editor.png?raw=true) |\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:38:59Z","updated_at":"2026-10-26T21:37:49Z","closed_at":"2026-10-26T21:37:45Z","merged_at":"2026-10-26T21:37:44Z","merge_commit_sha":"4893407fc5f813c64270df4d2f80bd670dfbd0fc","assignee":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"assignees":[{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercont